<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Spanish First Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1873 CE – 1874 CE · capital Madrid</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Spain's first republic, which went through four presidents in eleven months amid Carlist war, cantonal revolts and war in Cuba.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amadeo-i-of-spain">Amadeo</a> I abdicated on 11 February 1873, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corte">Cortes</a> proclaimed a republic, ending the monarchy of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sexenio-democratico">Sexenio Democrático</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estanislao-figueras">Estanislao Figueras</a> became the first head of the executive.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Republic was divided between unitary and federal republicans. A federal constitution dividing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> into states was drafted in 1873, largely by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-castelar">Emilio Castelar</a>, but never adopted. The government faced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-carlist-war">Third Carlist War</a>, the Cuban <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ten-years-war">Ten Years' War</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cantonal-rebellion">Cantonal Rebellion</a>, and its presidents, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estanislao-figueras">Figueras</a>, Pi, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicolas-salmeron">Nicolás Salmerón</a> and Emilio Castelar, followed in quick succession.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>On 3 January 1874 General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-pavia-y-rodriguez-de-alburquerque">Manuel Pavía</a> dissolved the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cortes">Cortes</a>. A unitary republic under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-serrano-1st-duke-of-la-torre">Serrano</a> followed until General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsenio-martinez-campos">Martínez Campos</a> proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-xii">Alfonso XII</a> in December 1874, beginning <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/restoration-spain">Restoration Spain</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/spanish-first-republic.jpg" alt="Spanish First Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Ignacio Gavira (original image), B1mbo (modifications) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Spain_(1873%E2%80%931874).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1873 CE – 1874 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Madrid</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Estanislao Figueras, Francesc Pi i Margall, Emilio Castelar</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>First Spanish Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1874&amp;focus=spanish-first-republic" aria-label="Spanish First Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4589 733 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Spanish First Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4909 989L4909 989M4909 989L4909 989M4909 989L4910 989M4909 989L4975 1081M4909 989L4991 1020M4909 989L4850 1088M4909 989L4889 1110M4909 989L4842 1116M4909 989L4910 1095"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4909 989h0M4909 989h0M4910 989h0M4975 1081h0M4991 1020h0M4850 1088h0M4889 1110h0M4842 1116h0M4910 1095h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4909 989h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4909 989h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Madrid. <a href="/atlas?year=1874&amp;focus=spanish-first-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
